# \[PATCH\] arm64: dts: rockchip: Remove non-functioning CPU OPPs from RK3576

**From:** Alexey Charkov

**Date:** Thu Oct 09 2025 - 08:34:51 EST

-   **Next message:** [Jinpu Wang: "Re: Hang on reboot in multi-core FreeBSD guest on Linux KVM host with Intel Sierra Forest CPU"](01790.html)
-   **Previous message:** [Lee Jones: "Re: (subset) \[PATCH\] mfd: altera-sysmgr: fix device leak on sysmgr regmap lookup"](01788.html)
-   **Next in thread:** [Heiko Stuebner: "Re: \[PATCH\] arm64: dts: rockchip: Remove non-functioning CPU OPPs from RK3576"](07068.html)
-   **Messages sorted by:** [\[ date \]](date.html#01789) [\[ thread \]](index.html#01789) [\[ subject \]](subject.html#01789) [\[ author \]](author.html#01789)

* * *

Drop the top-frequency OPPs from both the LITTLE and big CPU clusters on  
RK3576, as neither the opensource TF-A \[1\] nor the recent (after v1.08)  
binary BL31 images provided by Rockchip expose those.  

This fixes the problem \[2\] when the cpufreq governor tries to jump  
directly to the highest-frequency OPP, which results in a failed SCMI call  
leaving the system stuck at the previous OPP before the attempted change.  

\[1\] [https://github.com/ARM-software/arm-trusted-firmware/blob/master/plat/rockchip/rk3576/scmi/rk3576\_clk.c#L264-L304](https://github.com/ARM-software/arm-trusted-firmware/blob/master/plat/rockchip/rk3576/scmi/rk3576_clk.c#L264-L304)  
\[2\] [https://lore.kernel.org/linux-rockchip/CABjd4Yz4NbqzZH4Qsed3ias56gcga9K6CmYA+BLDBxtbG915Ag@xxxxxxxxxxxxxx/](https://lore.kernel.org/linux-rockchip/CABjd4Yz4NbqzZH4Qsed3ias56gcga9K6CmYA+BLDBxtbG915Ag@xxxxxxxxxxxxxx/)  

